cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Purpose-dependent drought accumulation scales for canopy monitoring and yield
  prediction in rainfed Turkish Thrace — code and derived data
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived data, please cite both the archive and
  the accompanying article.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kıvrak
    given-names: Cantekin
    affiliation: >-
      Atatürk Soil, Water and Agricultural Meteorology Research Institute,
      Kırklareli, Türkiye
    email: cantekin.kivrak@tarimorman.gov.tr
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
  - family-names: Şener
    given-names: Mehmet
    affiliation: 'Namık Kemal University, Biosystems Engineering, Tekirdağ, Türkiye'
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived, analysis-ready data reproducing the scale-selection,
  robustness, yield-prediction and spatial-aggregation results of the accompanying
  article. Cropland Landsat Vegetation Health Index (30 m, CORINE class 211 mask,
  alpha = 0.5) is evaluated against SPI and SPEI at five accumulation scales over
  seven districts of Turkish Thrace, 1985-2024.
keywords:
  - agricultural drought
  - SPEI
  - Landsat
  - Vegetation Health Index
  - time-scale selection
  - sunflower yield
  - Turkish Thrace
